WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:08.933
This walkthrough connects Discord using webhooks. A webhook is a private web address that posts into one channel. It takes about a minute for each channel.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:15.329
In Discord, hover over the channel you want reports in, and click the cog icon to edit the channel.

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:19.804
Open Integrations, then Webhooks, and press New Webhook.

00:00:20.004 --> 00:00:25.218
Give the webhook a name, then press Copy Webhook URL. Treat it like a password.

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:36.029
On the settings page, paste it into the matching box. Repeat for each channel. You can reuse one channel for several reports. Then press Save Discord, and Send test messages.

00:00:36.229 --> 00:00:42.403
That is Discord connected. Reports will post as they are filed, along with the daily scorecard.
